A||N||1||hoppe||88 heater hose placement||||1||
Z||000000||hoppe||01-27-2001||04:12 PM||||In the process of changing a leaking heater core. I can't remember which heater hose connects to which pipe under the car. Can anyone describe the proper connection for me? Also, has anyone ordered heater hoses form the Fiero store? Are they good quality?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mark||01-27-2001||05:26 PM||||If my memory is correct, the heater core hoses are two different sizes, therefore you shouldn't have a problem mixing them up.  <P>You should be aware that the heater core hoses from FS fit non-AC cars only.  If you have AC and you need to change the hoses, you're going to have to get a little creative (i.e., nobody sells these hoses)!<P>I tried standard (non-moulded) heater hose, but it kinked right at the chassis pipes.  My solution was to find two hoses that had a 90 degreee bend molded into one end (otherwise, these were straight hoses).  Put the molded bend down at the bottom where they connect to the chassis pipes and run the straight end to the heater core just like the original hoses.  Sorry, I long forgot the part numbers, but I purchased them at Pep-Boys a few years back.  It only took the counter guy a few minutes to find these hoses after I explained what I needed.<BR>[This message has been edited by Mark (edited 01-27-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Mark (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||1
